        "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nDisk temperature is shown as N/A in homarr when using OMV integration.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Make a OMV VM in pve and pass through a sata controller with a disc\n2. add the omv-extras addon and cpu-temp plugin\n3. make a homarr container and add the omv integration\n4. create a system health monitor item\n5. temperature is shown as N/A\n\n### Impact\n\ncannot see drive temperature when using omv integration\n\n### Additional information\n\n\nI have 2 drives one of which is virtual and so has no smart data however the other is physically passed through and as such has smart data readable to OMV and available in homarr through the network section in the inspect menu  is this file which has temperature\n\n[widget.healthMonitoring.getSystemHealthStatus.json](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/31122922/widget.healthMonitoring.getSystemHealthStatus.json)\n\n I think that the issue might be to do with the fact that sda is a virtual drive so maybe homarr ignores the rest\n\nOMV version: 8.5.6-1 synchrony\n\n# docker-compose.yaml\n  \n```\nservices:\n  homarr:\n    container_name: homarr\n    image: ghcr.io/homarr-labs/homarr:latest\n    restart: unless-stopped\n    volumes:\n      - /opt/homarr/appdata:/appdata\n    environment:\n      - SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY=${SECRET_ENCRYPTION_KEY}\n    ports:\n      - '7575:7575'\n\n```\n# \nsorry i cannot upload the yaml file for some reason\n\n### Version\n\n1.75.0\n\n### Installation method\n\nDocker Compose\n\n### Browser\n\nFirefox",
